"7aboir" <7aboir@gmail.com> wrote:

>Cannot make my putty connect to any of the (working) servers to display
>color. (any colored thing is displayed reversed white, just like my
>pet). (for instance, a jackal looks like my dog...)
>Any clue?

In PuTTY's settings menu, go to Connection->Data and set "Terminal-type
string" to "xterm-color" (instead of "xterm"). In NetHack, go to the
options menu and set the "color" option to "true".

